{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PTEC VAV Controller - Application 6603 (VAV with Hot Water Reheat)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6603-vav-hot-water-reheat",
  "short_model": "PTEC VAV Hot Water Reheat 6603",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6603",
    "Application 6603",
    "App 6603",
    "550-495PA",
    "Siemens VAV hot water reheat"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VAV terminal unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Pressure-independent single-duct VAV boxes with one or two floating hot water reheat valves on the Siemens BACnet PTEC terminal box controller 550-495PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6603 runs a single-duct VAV box with hot water reheat on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP. The cooling loop modulates the supply air damper; in heating the box holds minimum airflow or modulates airflow while one or two floating hot water valves modulate. REHEAT START/END and FLOW START/END set how airflow and reheat are sequenced on the heating loop.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F, cfm, ft²); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "The first valve uses DO 3/DO 4 and the optional second valve DO 5/DO 6; VALVE COUNT (AO 88) sets how many are used."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Terminal Box - VAV with Hot Water Reheat, Application 6603, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1164",
    "revision_date": "2014-10-27",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/SiIrcTNsG6YYbGZ2weDXRw/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the box to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, and reads room temperature, airflow, damper and reheat valve position and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "AIR VOLUME",
        "why": "Measured box airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 49",
        "name": "DMPR POS",
        "why": "Damper position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 53",
        "name": "VLV1 POS",
        "why": "Reheat valve 1 position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "VENT DMD MIN (AO 105) sets the occupied ventilation minimum airflow and can be adjusted by the field panel; the larger of it and the cooling or heating minimum is used.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6687."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "As shipped, the controller keeps all equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely."
    ]
  },
